<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Price equation (covariance form)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "For any population partitioned into entities i with fitness w_i and character value z_i, the change in the population mean character between generations equals the covariance of fitness with character plus the fitness-weighted mean of within-entity transmission change, each divided by mean fitness." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "\\bar{w}\\,\\Delta\\bar{z} = \\mathrm{Cov}(w_i, z_i) + \\mathrm{E}(w_i\\,\\Delta z_i)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: a well-defined parent-offspring mapping and finite means; no genetic or dynamical assumptions at all. Formal status: proved; it is an algebraic identity that holds for any partition of any population (Price 1970, 1972). Its content as a statement about selection depends on how the two terms are interpreted." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Not directly testable as an identity. Testable uses: partition a measured change in a trait into the selection and transmission terms in a pedigreed population and check that the terms are stable across alternative partitions." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "George R. Price (1970) Selection and Covariance" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/price-equation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-1809.1972.tb00764.x> .
}
